{"id": "sony-2026-06-17-005", "date": "2026-06-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 25, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["sony", "samsung_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": [], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.7, "reasons": ["多公司提及"]}, "title": "Samsung Launches Spidey Tracker Experience Ahead of Spider-Man™: Brand New Day", "content": "Samsung Electronics and Sony Pictures have launched the Spidey Tracker, an interactive fan experience powered by Galaxy devices, for Spider-Man: Brand New Day. Inspired by a tool created in the film by the character Ned Leeds to track Spider-Man’s movements using Galaxy devices, the experience has been brought to life as a dedicated website. Available […]", "sources": [{"name": "samsung_elec", "url": "https://news.samsung.com/global/samsung-launches-spidey-tracker-experience-ahead-of-spider-man-brand-new-day", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "samsung_elec-2026-06-17-006", "date": "2026-06-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 25, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["samsung_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Samsung Display demonstrates a 40,000 direct-emission OLED microdisplay", "content": "<p>Samsung Display is showing its latest OLED microdisplays at AWE USA 2026, including a 40,000 nits 1.3\" direct-emission OLED microdisplay, that the company refers to as RGB OLEDoS. This it the brightest OLED microdisplay demonstrated by SDC to date, and one of the brightest OLEDs ever developed (<a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/int-tech-developed-100000-nits-full-color-native-rgb-oled-microdisplay\">second only to INT Tech's displays</a>).</p><div>\n  \n  <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/site", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/samsung-display-demonstrates-40000-direct-emission-oled-microdisplay", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-17-007", "date": "2026-06-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 25, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "A spotlight on Visionox: a deep dive into the company's history, ViP and pTSF technologies, spin-outs, fabs and roadmaps", "content": "<p>Visionox is one of China's pioneering AMOLED producers, and arguably the industry's most technically ambitious second-tier player. Grown out of an OLED research group at Tsinghua University, the company built mainland China's first PMOLED line, its first AMOLED pilot line, and its first dedicated Gen-5.5 AMOLED mass-production line, and it currently holds somewhere around 10% of the global smartphone AMOLED market. By the end of 2024 it had shipped more than 240 million OLED panels cumulative", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/spotlight-visionox-deep-dive-companys-history-vip-technology-spin-outs-fabs-and", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "samsung_elec-2026-06-17-008", "date": "2026-06-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 25, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["samsung_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": [], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Chip supply chains shift: TSMC's capacity crunch reportedly pushes Google, Tesla, BYD toward Samsung", "content": "<p class=\"P1\" data-sourcepos=\"5:1-5:282;147-428\">Global chip buyers, including BYD, Google, AMD, and Tesla, are turning to Samsung Electronics as TSMC's advanced production lines remain fully booked, <em>Nikkei Asia</em> reported. The shift underscores how AI demand and supply-chain risk are reshaping where cutting-edge chips are made.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20260617VL215/samsung-tsmc-google-byd-tesla.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "boe-2026-06-17-009", "date": "2026-06-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 25, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["boe"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["expand", "[否定]mass production"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "BOE starts production at China's first 8.6G AMOLED line", "content": "BOE Technology Group has begun mass production at its Chengdu high-tech zone facility, a move that could reshape the supply of OLED displays for notebooks and tablets, while intensifying competition in a market where manufacturers across Asia are racing to expand higher-generation panel capacity for global electronics buyers.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20260617PD223/boe-chengdu-production-investment-amoled.html", "type": "rss"}]}
